      "writtenOn": "2026-08-21T10:40:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks — I may be missing something, so please let me know if you\u0027d prefer otherwise. My reasoning was to follow the DMTF model: ECCModeEnabled is defined under Processor.MemorySummary, covering all memory associated with the processor collectively. On that basis keeping the endpoint as the processor that owns the memory (Item.Cpu / Item.Accelerator) seemed semantically closer; pointing it at Item.Dimm would lose the \"memory belonging to this processor\" scoping.",
      "parentUuid": "61139629_2644bc85",
